We formalize when distributed training produces correct results. Definition 4 (Semantic Equivalence) . A distributed training configuration is semantically equivalent to single-device training if it produces the same sequence of parameter updates \Theta_{0},\Theta_{1},\Theta_{2},\ldots, up to floating-point differences arising from reduction order. Theorem 3 (Gradient Integrity) . For semantic equivalence, the gradient used for parameter update at step t must equal: G_{t}= rac{1}{B}\sum_{j=1}^{B}
